{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563109-homebrew-life-path-ideas","id":1563109,"title":"Homebrew Life Path Ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-14T14:51:07-07:00","id":1563109,"title":"Homebrew Life Path Ideas?","content":"What it says on the tin, this is a thread for any ideas regarding homebrewed Life Paths for V6.<br /> <br /> While I don't know what kind of skills and resources would be appropriate to give them, I have managed to come up with a basic concept,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Whipping Boy / Girl (Neonate)</b> - You may not be a hero, but the Beast hasn't stripped you of all your empathy quite yet. You've experienced enough of kindred society to know how ruthless it is towards the younger generations. Which is why you've taken it upon yourself to act as a martyr for the rest of your coterie. You are tough and stoic enough to take responsibility for any failures committed by your close allies, though you draw the line at anything that might warrant a death penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Slop Artist (Neonate)</b> - Vampires may have jumped the gun when they assumed the advancement of technology would threaten the Masquerade, but it's still not wise to leave such things entirely to chance. You have taken it upon yourself to flood social media with obviously false, cringe filled masquerade breaches, in an attempt to increase humanity's skepticism for when someone finally does get exposed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Urban Legend (Ancillae)</b> - You've been sloppy with upholding the masquerade, and it's garnered you a minor celebrity status among the kine. Rumors and myths about your activities have caused urban explorers and cryptid hunters to come snooping around your domain, in the hopes of capturing proof of your existence. Additionally, your notoriety has had a negative impact on your relationship with the governing body of kindred society, hindering your opportunities for continued advancement.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T03:14:17-07:00","id":1563169,"title":"","content":"I only know the life path systems in Mutant Chronicles and Traveller. Both of them were randomized, you could have some crazy results.<br /> <br /> In MC you could end up with one PC having a social status of 10 and the other 1. So pretty much Elon Musk equivalent teams up with Bob, the destitute crack addict other crack addicts look down on. Together they fight extra dimensional demons. And crime.<br /> <br /> In MC you could also end up as a demon but the odds were low.<br /> <br /> In traveler you could die in character creation.<br /> <br /> In both systems you could loose your job and have it rough for a while.<br /> <br /> Your last suggestions sounds more like a flaw but it's a cool concept. Should come with a moniker for the legend. 'The animal man downtown'. 'the slit-mouthed woman's. 'the tall man in the darkness'. Let's you ram it in wherever the PCs go. They go to a party and five separate people dress up as 'the mothman of Clivesville'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T15:27:53-07:00","id":1563197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563109-homebrew-life-path-ideas?p=1563169#post1563169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your last suggestions sounds more like a flaw but it's a cool concept. Should come with a moniker for the legend. 'The animal man downtown'. 'the slit-mouthed woman's. 'the tall man in the darkness'. Let's you ram it in wherever the PCs go. They go to a party and five separate people dress up as 'the mothman of Clivesville'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vision was that they take up the life of a hermit, living on the fringes of the Prince's domain. Far enough away that they don't warrant a blood hunt, but close enough that they aren't completely irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T15:50:01-07:00","id":1563201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563109-homebrew-life-path-ideas?p=1563169#post1563169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only know the life path systems in Mutant Chronicles and Traveller. Both of them were randomized, you could have some crazy results.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the current Playtest a Life Path is a package of 5 skills and 3 Backgrounds tied by what kind of life you were living for a given period.<br /> <br /> You get a number of dots to distribute within this list. And they're not random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}